.SH NAME
tcarecv \- Trusted Collective daemon task for receiving newly generated records of critical information
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBtcarecv\fR \fIblocks_group_number\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBtcarecv\fR is a background "daemon" task that receives new critical
information records multicast by user nodes of the TC application identified
by \fIblocks_group_number\fR.  It records those assertions in a database for
future processing by \fBtcacompile\fR.  It is spawned automatically by
\&\fBtcaadmin\fR in response to the 's' command that starts operation of
the TC authority function for this application on the local node, and
it is terminated by \fBtcaadmin\fR in response to an 'x' (STOP) command.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.IX Header "EXIT STATUS"
.IP """0""" 4
.IX Item """0"""
\&\fBtcarecv\fR terminated, for reasons noted in the \fBion.log\fR file.  If this
termination was not commanded, investigate and solve the problem identified
in the log file and use \fBtcaadmin\fR to restart \fBtcarecv\fR.
.IP """1""" 4
.IX Item """1"""
\&\fBtcarecv\fR was unable to attach to DTKA operations, probably because
\&\fBtcaadmin\fR has not yet been run.
.SH FILES
.IX Header "FILES"
No configuration files are needed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IX Header "ENVIRONMENT"
No environment variables apply.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.IX Header "DIAGNOSTICS"
The following diagnostics may be issued to the \fBion.log\fR log file:
.IP "tcarecv can't attach to DTKA." 4
.IX Item "tcarecv can't attach to DTKA."
\&\fBtcaadmin\fR has not yet initialized the authority database for this TC
application.
.SH BUGS
.IX Header "BUGS"
Report bugs to <https://github.com/nasa\-jpl/ION\-DTN/issues>
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBtcaadmin\fR\|(1), \fBtc\fR\|(3), \fBtcarc\fR\|(5)
